<title>GERMANY: SPEED SKATING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SPEED SKATING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>INZELL, Germany 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on Friday on the</p>
<p>first day of the final World Cup speed skating event of the</p>
<p>season:</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p>500 metres</p>
<p>1. Kyoko Shimazaki (Japan) 40.30 seconds</p>
<p>2. Marianne Timmer (Netherlands) 40.39</p>
<p>3. Tomomi Okazaki (Japan) 40.43</p>
<p>4. Sabine Voelker (Germany) 40.61</p>
<p>5. Susan Auch (Canada) 40.69</p>
<p>6. Ruihong Xue (China) 40.70</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>500 metres</p>
<p>1. Hiroyasu Shimizu (Japan) 36.57 seconds</p>
<p>2. Manabu Horii (Japan) 36.76</p>
<p>3. Sergei Klevshenya (Russia) 37.18</p>
<p>4. Junichi Inoue (Japan) 37.28</p>
<p>5. Casey Fitzrandolph (U.S.) 37.35</p>
<p>6. Mike Ireland (Canada) 37.38</p>
<p>5,000 metres</p>
<p>1. Rintje Ritsma (Netherlands) 6:45.70 minutes (track record)</p>
<p>2. Gianni Romme (Netherlands) 6:49.44</p>
<p>3. Ids Postma (Netherlands) 6:54.80</p>
<p>4. Frank Dittrich (Germany) 6:55.24</p>
<p>5. Bob de Jong (Netherlands) 6:57.21</p>
<p>6. Kjell Storelid (Norway) 6:57.87</p>
</text>
